# Branch before commit or push

Do the work on a new branch off `main`. Do not edit `main` directly.

Leave the changes uncommitted until the user explicitly asks to commit. Do not push, open a pull request, or merge until the user explicitly asks.

The branch is how they preview the diff and the running site first. A local preview server is enough. Publishing to `main` or to a release tag happens only after they say to commit and push.
